vival Evaluation in Japan (CASE-J) trial</article-title><source>J Epidemiol</source><year>2005</year><volume>15</volume><fpage>38</fpage><lpage>40</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15762092</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.2188/jea.15.38</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B16"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Franke</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Kommers</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Van</surname><given-names>WE</given-names></name><name><surname>Lucasson</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Beek</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Van den</surname><given-names>HH</given-names></name><name><surname>Van</surname><given-names>WC</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>General practice registrars and research &#x02013; attitudes toward participation</article-title><source>Aust Fam Physician</source><year>2008</year><volume>37</volume><fpage>276</fpage><lpage>279</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">18398529</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B17"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hummers-Pradier</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Scheidt-Nave</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Martin</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Heinemann</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Kochen</surname><given-names>MM</given-names></name><name><surname>Himmel</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Simply no time? Barriers to GPs' participation in primary health care research</article-title><source>Fam Pract</source><year>2008</year><volume>25</volume><fpage>105</fpage><lpage>112</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">18417465</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1093/fampra/cmn015</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B18"><citation citation-type="journa